  "descriptions": [
    {
      "source": "DeFiHackLabs",
      "text": "Unrestricted Approval. Lost: $820k(2500BNB)"
    },
    {
      "source": "DeFiHackLabs explorer",
      "text": "Public approve() This contract has a function called approve that grants the caller of the function access to the $META tokens without any restriction. Vulnerable code snippet: Attack tx: invest https://bscscan.com/tx/0xdb01fa33bf5b79a3976ed149913ba0a18ddd444a072a2f34a0042bf32e4e7995 withdraw https://bscscan.com/tx/0x41853747231dcf01017cf419e6e4aa86757e59479964bafdce0921d3e616cc67 Analysis: https://twitter.com/PeckShieldAlert/status/1645980197987192833 https://twitter.com/Phalcon_xyz/status/1645963327502204929"
    },
    {
      "source": "SlowMist",
      "text": "MetaPoint ($POT) on BSC was hacked with a loss of $920K. The root cause is that users will create a new contract to hold their funds each time they deposit $POT, but the contract has a public approve function to transfer all users' assets."
    },
    {
      "source": "RevertIQ",
      "text": "MetaPoint on BNB Chain was drained through public approval abuse on 2023-04-11. The on-chain record shows 11 contracts granting unlimited POT allowance to an exploit contract, with reported losses around 2,515 BNB. An externally callable approval function let an attacker set unlimited POT allowance from 11 MetaPoint-associated contracts without any caller authorization, after which the attacker used transferFrom to drain the balances."
    }
  ],
